<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Soloverse Rulebook Hub</title>
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0f1015" />

    <!-- Pure, native PWA registration. No custom code download hooks to break on mobile webviews -->
    <script is:inline>
      if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
        window.addEventListener('load', () => {
          navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js', { scope: '/' })
            .then(reg => console.log('PWA Registered:', reg.scope))
            .catch(err => console.error('PWA Failed:', err));
        });
      }
    </script>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- =============================================================== -->

		<!-- THE REACTIVE THEME & ROTATION OPTION INTERFACE CONTROLLER BUTTONS -->
    <div class="theme-toggle-container">
        <button id="theme-toggle-btn" class="theme-btn">☀️ Light Mode</button>
    </div>
	
		<div class="image-container">
			<img
				src="/assets/images/layouts/soloverse-logo.png" 
				alt="Centred Image"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
		</div>

		<h1>Soloverse Rulebook Hub</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
        You'll notice that there are several Coloured Boxes below.
        Please note that each Box represents part of the Soloverse, that is to say, a different set of Game Rules.
        So First, You'll need to choose which Game You want to Play.
        Here at Soloverse, we recommend beginning with the Tutorial Game Crazy 8's as that the most know of all the games.
        Once a Game has been selected, You will find 2 specific Rulebook Types in each Game:
    </p>
        <ol type="1">
            <li>XX-A Soloverse - GAME NAME [Game Rulebook]. This Rulebook explains how to Play the Chosen Game.</li>
            <li>XX-B Soloverse - GAME NAME [Definitions Rulebook]. This Rulebook explains what each Card in the Game does.</li>
        </ol>
    <p class="subtitle">
        Having these Rulebooks split helps in quick referencing the Card Effects, because generally You'll need the Game Rules less than the these Card Definitions.
        And since my Card Rules are Digital, I am able to alter their Definitions, allowing for more Game Modes to be added, expanding how much fun You can have in the Soloverse!
        Also know that each additional Game that has been added to the Game, has kept the Card Definitions as close to the Original in the Tutorual Game: Crazy 8's as possible.
    </p>

<!-- ==================== PART 1: THE DYNAMIC GAME CARDS GRID ==================== -->
    <div class="grid">
        {renderedGames.map((game, index) => {
            const titleColor = game.boxColor === "#fff200" ? "#111216" : "#ffffff";
            const textShadowRule = game.boxColor === "#fff200" ? "none" : "0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.6)";

            return (
                <button 
                    class="game-card selector-trigger" 
                    data-target={`vault-${game.id}`}
                    style="text-align: left; width: 100%; border: none; padding: 0; cursor: pointer; display: block; overflow: hidden;"
                >
                    <div class="game-header" style={`background-color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 4px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.25);`}>
                        <h2 class="game-title" style={`color: ${titleColor}; text-shadow: ${textShadowRule};`}>
                            {game.title}
                        </h2>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="box-contents">
                        <p style="margin: 0; padding: 10px; color: #ced4da; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                            👉 Tap to open the live Rulebook and Card Database interface.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </button>
            );
        })}
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== NEW SPLIT-VIEW LIVE RULEBOOK PANELS ==================== -->
    <div class="vault-panels-holder" style="margin-top: 40px;">
        {renderedGames.map((game, index) => {
            const Rules = game.RulesComponent;
            const Cards = game.CardsComponent;
            const Solo = game.SoloComponent;

            return (
                <div id={`vault-${game.id}`} class={`game-panel ${index === 0 ? '' : 'hidden'}`}>
                    <div class="panel-accent-header" style={`border-left: 6px solid ${game.boxColor}; background: #16171e; padding: 15px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 20px;`}>
                        <h2 style="margin: 0; color: #fff;">{game.title} - Operational Database</h2>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="split-view">
                        <!-- Column 1: Core Rulebook -->
                        <section class="content-block">
                            <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; padding-bottom: 10px;`}>📜 Game Rulebook</h3>
                            <div class="text-layer">
                                {Rules ? <Rules /> : <p>No core rulebook document compiled for this variant layout yet.</p>}
                            </div>
                        </section>

                        <!-- Column 2: Card Definitions & Solo Rules -->
                        <section class="content-block">
                            <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; padding-bottom: 10px;`}>🃏 Card Definitions & Reference</h3>
                            <div class="text-layer">
                                {Cards ? <Cards /> : <p>No card database structure linked yet.</p>}
                                
                                {Solo && (
                                    <div class="solo-layer" style="margin-top: 30px; border-top: 2px dashed #2a2d3d; padding-top: 20px;">
                                        <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; margin-top: 0;`}>🕹️ Solo Mode Rules</h3>
                                        <Solo />
                                    </div>
                                )}
                            </div>
                        </section>
                    </div>
                </div>
            );
        })}
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PART 2: THE UPCOMING PIPELINE STACK ==================== -->
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="section-divider">
            🛠️ In Development Blueprint Stack ({upcomingGames.length} Variants Pipeline)
        </div>

        <div class="grid">
            {upcomingGames.map((upcoming) => (
                <div class="blueprint-card">
                    <h2 class="blueprint-title">{upcoming.title}</h2>
                    <div class="status-badge">📦 Under Construction</div>
                </div>
            ))}
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PART 3: THE SMART PWA INSTALLATION OVERLAY ==================== -->
    <div id="pwa-banner" class="pwa-install-banner">
        <div class="pwa-header">
            <div class="pwa-title">📱 Add Soloverse to Home Screen</div>
            <button id="pwa-close" class="pwa-close-btn" aria-label="Close popup">×</button>
        </div>
        <div id="pwa-instructions" class="pwa-body">
            <!-- Content will be auto-generated by your script layer -->
        </div>
        <div class="pwa-action-row">
            <button id="pwa-dismiss" class="pwa-btn pwa-btn-secondary">Not Now</button>
            <button id="pwa-action-btn" class="pwa-btn pwa-btn-primary" style="display: none;">Install App</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SOLOVERSE VAULT CENTRAL STYLING ENGINE ==================== -->
    <style is:inline>
        /* 1. GLOBAL LAYOUT FRAMEWORK CONSTRAINTS */
        body { 
            background-color: #0f1015; 
            color: #e4e6eb; 
            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; 
            margin: 0; 
            padding: 20px; 
            max-width: 100vw;
            overflow-x: hidden;
        }
        
        .vault-container { 
            max-width: 1400px; 
            margin: 0 auto; 
            width: 100%;
        }

        header { 
            text-align: center; 
            margin-bottom: 40px; 
            border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; 
            padding-bottom: 25px; 
        }

        /* 1B. THEME PILL TOGGLE INTERFACE CONTROLS */
        .theme-toggle-container {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: flex-start;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
        }

        .theme-btn {
            background: #171922;
            color: #ffffff;
            border: 1px solid #2d3139;
            padding: 10px 16px;
            border-radius: 50px; 
            font-weight: 700;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            display: inline-flex; 
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s, transform 0.1s;
        }

        .theme-btn:hover {
            border-color: #3b82f6;
            background: #1c1d26;
        }

        .theme-btn:active { 
            transform: scale(0.97); 
        }

        /* 2. DYNAMIC SELECTION CARDS GRID PROFILE */
        .grid { 
            display: grid; 
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); 
            gap: 20px; 
            width: 100%; 
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .game-card {
            background: #16171e;
            border-radius: 16px; 
            overflow: hidden;    
            border: 1px solid #2d3139; 
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
            transition: transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), box-shadow 0.2s ease;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
        }
        .game-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-4px);
            box-shadow: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
        }

        .game-header {
            padding: 24px 20px;
            text-align: center;
            position: relative; 
            /* 🚀 THE ZOOM FIX: Pre-rounds the inner color block so fractional scaling remainders can't bleed out */
            border-top-left-radius: 14px;
            border-top-right-radius: 14px;
            background-clip: padding-box; /* Forces the background color to respect inner boundary layers */
        }
        .game-header::after {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            inset: 0;
            background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35));
            pointer-events: none; 
        }

        .game-title {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 10; 
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1.15rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.03em;
        }

        .box-contents {
            padding: 20px;
            background: #1c1e27; 
            flex-grow: 1;
        }

        /* 3. SPLIT-VIEW OPERATIONS INTERFACE DASHBOARD */
        .vault-panels-holder { width: 100%; }
        .game-panel { 
            animation: vaultFadeIn 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); 
            width: 100%;
        }
        .hidden { display: none !important; }

        /* ==========================================================================
           3. SPLIT-VIEW OPERATIONS INTERFACE DASHBOARD (VIEWPORT-LOCKED ENGINE)
           ========================================================================= */
        .vault-panels-holder { 
            width: 100%; 
        }
        
        .game-panel { 
            animation: vaultFadeIn 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); 
            width: 100%;
        }
        
        .hidden { 
            display: none !important; 
        }

        /* 📱 DEFAULT PORTRAIT MODE: Automatically stacks top and bottom */
        .split-view { 
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px; 
            margin-top: 20px; 
            width: 100%;
            /* Constrains the total split-view area to a manageable mobile phone canvas */
            height: 75vh; 
        }

        /* 🕹️ LOCKED MULTI-SCROLL INDEPENDENT COLUMNS */
        .content-block { 
            background: #16171e; 
            border: 1px solid #2a2d3d; 
            padding: 20px; 
            border-radius: 8px; 
            min-width: 0; 
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            
            /* CRITICAL: Activates isolated native momentum scrolling per column box */
            flex: 1;
            overflow-y: auto; 
            -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; 
            
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        }

        /* 🎮 AUTOMATIC LANDSCAPE MODE BREAKPOINT (SIDE-BY-SIDE SIDE PANEL ENGINE) */
        @media screen and (min-width: 600px) and (orientation: landscape) { 
            .split-view { 
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; /* Splitting the screen perfectly left and right */
                gap: 25px;
                /* Expands the columns to comfortably consume the available table view estate */
                height: 80vh; 
            }
            
            .content-block {
                height: 100%; /* Forces both blocks to match the height grid wrapper frame exactly */
            }
        }

        /* Clean up internal text spacing layout within the scroll zones */
        .text-layer { 
            line-height: 1.6; 
            color: #ced4da; 
            font-size: 0.98rem;
            flex-grow: 1;
        }

        .text-layer { 
            line-height: 1.6; 
            color: #ced4da; 
            font-size: 0.98rem;
        }

        /* 4. PRESERVES YOUR NESTED VISUAL RULEBOOK BOX STYLING FLUSH LAYOUTS */
        .rules-box { 
            margin-bottom: 20px; 
            width: 100%; 
            box-sizing: border-box; 
        }
        .card-header-block {
            background: #20222e;
            padding: 12px 16px;
            border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #2a2d3d;
        }
        
        .rules-box, .discards-box, .compatibility-box, .restriction-box {
